Z||000000||My7Fieros||03-16-2001||05:07 PM||||Well I just had the none to fun expierience of putting a new water pump on my 86 SE (V6) 4 speed. AAARRRGGG!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Question though, this water pump that I took off had a metal nipple with a hose comming out of it leading to the rear wall (trunk side)...my other Fieros have this hole blocked off....what is it? I put it on and connected the hose like it was on the old one...extra work no doubt...any ideas what it does?<BR>Also no from time to time the new pump makes a strange noise...kinda sounds like the noise a seal makes (no way to describe it)...oh well, runs fine. Thanx, M7F<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||03-16-2001||06:45 PM||||It's the coolant return from the heater core up front...<P>For the 1987-later V6 Fieros, they eliminated a separate return line+hose, from heater core back to the water pump.  Instead, they fed  return coolant from the heater core into the main coolant line on the passenger side of the car... and plugged the port in the water pump.<P>Good idea - saved a couple parts, and probably saved GM some $   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>No idea about the noise, sorry - haunted, maybe? <P>  <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||03-17-2001||02:32 PM||||Check your belts for the "seal" barking noise you might just have to tighten them up a bit.||||reg||3
